  "title": "Silvia F NDE 4823",
  "date": "febbraio 2001",
  "content": "It happened four months after I got my driving license. I was going to the doctor to get the vaccine for asthma. At a sharp bend, I left the road. I do not remember if it was sleep caused by medications, which I was taking (for asthma), or speed (I remember I was in the third gear) - I just know I went straight! Suddenly I saw myself enveloped by a huge white light. At first, I did not understand where I was. I woke up after a while, or at least I thought so, and I saw the car destroyed - glass all around, a concrete pole (it was a field of grapes or something similar) embedded in the glass front two inches from my face and another pole above my head at a few centimeters. I saw the mess I was before but I noticed that I wasn't injured I hadn't even a scratch! I was in shock as I reached the first home I found and I asked for help! I continued shivering and they gave me about five cups of chamomile tea, but I could not calm down. I saw later, when my father arrived, the condition the care was in. The car was totaled but we managed to fix it! According to me someone up there really loved me and gave me a hand - maybe it was not yet my time!",
